* provenance: 2N5457, 2N5458, 2N5459 JFET general-purpose N-channel depletion amplifiers, datasheet 2N5457/D, onsemi (Fairchild), https://www.onsemi.com/download/data-sheet/pdf/2n5457-d.pdf; read from memory of the electrical characteristics table, not re-checked against the PDF from this machine, so every value is UNVERIFIED until compared with the sheet
* fit: the sheet gives the 2N5458 as IDSS 2.0 to 9.0 mA (VDS = 15 V, VGS = 0), VGS(off) -1.0 to -7.0 V, forward transfer admittance 1500 to 5500 umho (1 kHz), Ciss 4.5 pF typical and Crss 1.5 pF maximum. The sheet states ranges, not one value, so the model sits at the mid-range: IDSS 5.5 mA and Vto -4 V (DERIVED: Beta = IDSS / Vto^2 = 0.344 mA/V^2, which gives gfs = 2 * IDSS / |Vto| = 2.75 mS, inside the sheet range). CGD = 1.5p is the Crss maximum and CGS = 3p is Ciss 4.5 pF minus CGD (DERIVED). No channel-length modulation: the sheet states no output-conductance value that this fit uses. Real parts vary across the whole range, so a RAT built with one differs from this model
* author: 4esv
* license: MIT

.model J2N5458 NJF(Beta=3.44e-4 Vto=-4 CGS=3p CGD=1.5p)
